From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:04:39 -0400
Subject: feat: the owner's round after beta 4: issues 8, 11, 12, drags, the
 list

The owner's requests of 2026-10-22, after 0.3.0 beta 4:

- A Copy Link button in the address field (copy-link L7, settings T28,
  toolbar T46; GitHub issue 11): Chromium's Copy Link action shown as a
  page action before the star. A click copies the clean link, as Cmd-Shift-C
  does; an Option-click (Alt-click) the Markdown link. A preference, on by
  default, hides it. A little window has it too, with the toast that
  confirms it (GitHub issue 48).
- Essentials of a Space's own (ADR 0028; spaces B6, sessions S8; GitHub
  issue 8): a tab pinned in a Space with an Independent session is that
  Space's essential, in its jar and shown in it alone, which shows no
  shared essential. The session restore marks it, a Space whose session is
  turned off makes its essentials its pins, and a deleted Space's go where
  its tabs go. The warning that pinning such a tab signed it out, its toast
  and its preference are gone (sessions S33, settings T25 withdrawn).
- A drag that rests on another Space's chip for half a second switches the
  window there, the dragged rows filed under it first, and goes on into
  that Space's list (spaces B12); a drop beside a chip takes the nearest,
  and in the dots form only the lit chip grows.
- A folder's header dragged onto another folder's header goes into it,
  whole, and between an open folder's rows it goes there; a nested
  folder's header drags too (folders F10, F38, F39;
  TabStripModel::MoveFolderInto).
- A close shows the Space's most recent row only while it is in the
  sidebar's view, else the row below, so the list no longer jumps (tabs
  R33).
- A list taller than the sidebar scrolls past its last row by half its
  height (sidebar Y30).
- The "+ New Tab" row takes the tab rows' hover tint under the pointer and
  the selected row's fill while pressed (sidebar Y32; GitHub issue 12).
- A scroll moves the hover to the row it brings under the resting pointer,
  and ends a hover card's wait (sidebar Y31, pins H26).
- After a relaunch every folder looked grey: a header no longer takes the
  slept look (tabs R7).
- A link's tab opens just below its page: "Show tabs under the tab that
  opened them" is off by default (settings T26, tabs R57).
- A pin sent home tells its row, which shows the home's title at once; a
  pin made on the New Tab page takes its first web page as home (pins H1,
  H3).
- A link from a tab in a folder nested in a pinned folder leaves for the
  rows under the line, so the folder stays pinned (folders F38).
- The hover card's resource line (pins H25): after 2 seconds on a tab, the
  card's foot gives its memory, CPU and network rate, read every second,
  or "Asleep"; resource attribution for memory and CPU, the task manager
  for the network rate, run only while a line is due.
- A row dragged across the Clear line takes the pin of the side it is
  dropped on, where it is dropped, and the line is drawn during the drag
  where the drop would leave it (pins H14; BACKLOG S-271). A loose row
  dropped among the pins stayed loose and the run's last pin showed under
  the line; a pin dropped among the loose rows stayed a pin.
- The Copy Link button's press ends its ripple as a button's does, so its
  fill goes with the pointer (copy-link L7; BACKLOG S-273, GitHub issue
  11): a page action's press waits for a bubble that Copy Link never opens.

Tests: CopyLinkTest.*; SpaceWindowTest's own-essential tests and
IsolationMarkTest.PinningAWorkTabKeepsItInWorksSession; TabDropTest's five
chip tests and SwitcherRulesTest.ATabDropTakesTheNearestChip;
FolderTabsTest.AFolderDraggedOntoAFoldersHeaderGoesIntoIt and four more,
TabStripModelTest.MoveFolderInto*; SidebarClickTest.ACloseKeepsTheListWhereItIs,
AListScrollsHalfItsHeightPastItsLastRow and
APinSentHomeShowsItsHomeInItsRow; FolderTabsTest.AScrollMovesTheHoverToTheRowUnderIt;
SidebarClickTest.TheNewTabRowLightsUnderThePointer;
HoverCardPictureTest.AScrollDropsACardWaitingToShow and
ACardShowsItsTabsUseAfterAPause; TabResourceLineTest.*;
PinnedRunTest.ALinkFromANestedPinnedFolderLeavesItInTheRun and
ARowDraggedAcrossTheLineTakesThePinThere; and
stedding::test::WaitForRowsToSettleAtFramePace for a row moved into a
nested folder.

Why: the owner's notes on beta 4 and three GitHub issues the owner chose
to build; each closes a way the sidebar, the pins or the Spaces did not do
what a person expected.
Removable when: never; the next re-cut folds each into the patch that owns
its feature (Spaces, sessions, pins, folders, the sidebar, the toolbar,
the hover card).
